    "body": "## Motivation\n\nMiniCPM-V-2.6 pads image slices to the largest patch count in the batch. `VisionAscendAttention` removes those padded rows before FIA, then scatters the compact result into an output allocated with `torch.empty_like(q)`. Only valid rows are written, so padding retains uninitialized memory (or stale graph workspace contents).\n\nDuring an Ascend A3 reproduction, one image produced slice lengths `[1014, 1036, 1036]`: 3086 valid rows in a 3108-row padded tensor. The first vision attention output had no nonfinite values in valid rows but 49 in padding. Nonfinite values subsequently appeared in the resampler output, and greedy decoding repeated `!` without reaching EOS. Requests without an explicit output limit continued decoding.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Zero the padded output before restoring FIA results, for both multiple sequences and a single padded sequence. The unpadded path continues returning the FIA output directly.\n- Add deterministic regression coverage using NaN-filled allocations and graph workspaces. Check valid Q/K/V packing, restored results, and zero padding across eager, metadata, and graph paths, including an unpadded control.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n```bash\npython -m pytest test/registered/unit/layers/attention/test_vision_backend_selection.py -q\n```\n\n- Community `main` Python source: **25 passed** with the fix.\n- The 9 added parameter combinations against the original implementation: **6 failed, 3 passed**. All padded combinations fail; unpadded controls pass.\n- Ascend A3 / CANN 9.1.0 B083 image (`8b3bf500d746d3140e8b25332d2207429aab0373`) with this runtime fix: all **6 MiniCPM-V-2.6 tests passed in 96.231 s**, including mixed batch, single image, multiple images, multiple turns, video, and prefix cache reuse. Used the `TestMiniCPMV4Server` class from the Ascend test module, whose model is MiniCPM-V-2.6, with local weights and the original generation limits. This end-to-end run validates the fix on the B083 runtime; the unit suite above validates the current target source.\n- The previously failing single-image response completed naturally after 42 tokens with `finish_reason=stop`.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo throughput benchmark. The fix adds zeroing only when restoring a padded output. In the end-to-end run, the mixed-batch test completed in 7.839 s and the single-image test in 0.902 s.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Ruff formatting and lint, isort, and `git diff --check` passed for changed files.\n- [x] Added regression tests and verified failure before / success after the fix.\n- [x] Validated MiniCPM-V-2.6 outputs on Ascend A3.\n- [x] No public API or configuration changes requiring documentation.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38196887759](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38196887759)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38196887510](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38196887510)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38196887805](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38196887805)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
